{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZavXmVe5rvGPAMwnvzp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me check how many files I've read and confirm I'm within the retrieval budget:\n\nI've read 5 distinct files so far (Shipment.kt, ShipmentController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ShipmentControllerTest.kt, ApiExceptions.kt, GlobalExceptionHandler.kt, ApiError.kt, OrderController.kt). I'm approaching my 15-file limit, so I should proceed to the design phase now.\n\n## ANALYSIS SUMMARY:\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED status, succeeds without change on re-confirm of already CONFIRMED, returns 409 for CANCELLED shipments, and returns 404 for missing shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model at `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` with three statuses: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController at `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20-56` implements POST/GET/LIST operations\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository at `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` with save, findById, findAll, existsById\n- Error handling: ApiException hierarchy with ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) at `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` converts exceptions to ApiError envelope\n- Tests at `/sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to ApiError envelope\n- Error codes live in ErrorCode enum in ApiError.kt\n- StatusCodes: 201 for create, 409 for conflict, 404 not found, 200 for success\n- Successful responses return the entity in the body\n- Tests use MockMvc, test both success and error paths\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. ShipmentController.kt - add confirm endpoint\n2. ApiError.kt - add new error code for invalid shipment status\n3. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - add tests for confirm behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n- If idempotency isn't correct, retries will fail\n- Missing CANCELLED state validation could allow invalid transitions\n- New error code must match the ErrorCode enum\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket clearly specifies all four cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the ErrorCode enum for when a shipment cannot be confirmed due to its status.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Takes shipmentId as path variable\n   - Looks up the shipment; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates status to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is already CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent)\n   - Returns the shipment with 200 OK\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and transitions to confirmed` - CREATED → CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm of already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` - CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (no change)\n   - `confirming a cancelled shipment is rejected with conflict` - CANCELLED → 409 with error code\n   - `confirming a non-existent shipment returns not found` - 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could implement confirm in the repository as a method (e.g., `confirmShipment(id: String): Shipment?`) instead of putting the logic in the controller. This would be cleaner separation of concerns but adds unnecessary complexity for this simple in-memory store. Keeping it in the controller follows the existing pattern (create does validation in controller).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller receives | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|------------------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | Find by ID | save(updated shipment) | 200 + Shipment | Normal response |\n| CONFIRMED retry | Find by ID | (no write) | 200 + Shipment | Normal response (idempotent) |\n| CANCELLED | Find by ID | (no write) | 409 + error | ConflictException caught by handler |\n| Unknown ID | (not found) | (no write) | 404 + error | ResourceNotFoundException caught by handler |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirm_created_moves_to_confirmed`: Create S-1 in CREATED, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED in response and persisted\n2. `confirm_confirmed_idempotent`: Create S-2 in CREATED, confirm twice, verify second confirm returns 200 and status unchanged\n3. `confirm_cancelled_rejected`: Manually save S-3 with CANCELLED status, confirm it, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS code\n4. `confirm_missing_rejected`: Try to confirm S-missing, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":20369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0a284ac-7322-490d-a4c6-da3850736047","uuid":"2518b388-148b-47ad-9dab-5c29696c03c9","timestamp":"2026-09-30T11:59:36.087Z","request_id":"req_011CfZavXMC8gcce8VbHMeHW"}
